    "html": "<p>A <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"45 \\mathrm{~W}\"></span> electric heater is used to maintain a liquid of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.75 \\mathrm{~kg}\"></span> at a constant temperature. When the heater is switched off, the temperature of the liquid is observed to decrease at an initial rate of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.030 \\mathrm{~K} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\"></span>. What is the specific heat capacity of the liquid?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~kg}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.5 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~kg}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.8 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~kg}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~kg}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
